Restore dropped segment bases in FUN_0000_fe47 (FISTDATA data-path detector).

fe47 chdir's to the data dir (STRSEG:0x9b/0x9c) via the CRT drive/dir helper FUN_1000_23a5 (AH=3Bh),
records a flag at DGROUP:0x16c6, and on the copy path stores the drive letter at STRSEG:0x158. Ghidra
dropped the DS=DGROUP base on the `movb [0x16c6]` stores (-> host deref 0x16c6 -> SIGSEGV), the ES=[0x70]
base on `mov es:[0x158],al`, and the DGROUP base on the `lcall [0x5c]/[0x60]` service-vector reads.
Rebase all: DGROUP 0x16c6/0x5c/0x60 and STRSEG 0x158.

NB (decompile update): the chdir helper 0x23a5 and the drive-set helper 0x23bf -- previously unresolved
near-calls rendered as no-op func_0x0001XXXX stubs -- are now real functions (FUN_1000_23a5/23bf: seeded
via SeedServiceVecs as reloc-section-0x174 display-list-element method vectors, which they double as).
They now execute real INT 21h AH=3Bh chdir / AH=0Eh set-drive marshalling; our shim accepts chdir and
open_ci searches the data dirs directly regardless of CWD, so behaviour is unchanged. The copy-path
`if (bVar5)` blocks stay dead (bVar5 = the dropped chdir CF, defaults false == the faithful reached path);
their stores are rebased anyway for correctness. Class: DS=DGROUP / [0x70] dynamic-segment base loss.

